   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "וְאִם הָיוּ שֶׁל יְחִידִים וְכוּ׳. אָמַר רַב יוֹסֵף, תָּנֵי רַבִּי: הָיוּ שְׁלֹשָׁה — אֲסוּרִין.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «And if» the courtyards belonged «to individuals,» i.e., if only one person lived in each courtyard, they are not required to establish an eiruv. «Rav Yosef said: Rabbi» Yehuda HaNasi «teaches» that if «there were three» people living in the two courtyards, whether two people lived in the outer courtyard and one person in the inner one, or two people lived in the inner courtyard and one person lived in the outer one, «they are prohibited» from carrying without an eiruv."
  }
